 "review_status": "pending-human-review",
 "description": "Manifest tree vectors (format 1). Each case builds a tree from a list of files and gives the expected root hash, the number of distinct nodes and the nodes in walk order (a directory's own nodes - index first, then its pages - followed by its subdirectories in name order). canonical is the exact node text (UTF-8, no trailing newline); it is listed for nodes up to 4096 bytes, larger nodes give size and hash only. Cases with error must be rejected with that path error kind. decode_invalid lists node byte strings that a strict decoder must reject.",
 "inputs": "files: {path, content (UTF-8 text), mode (default 420)}; the file's hash is sha256 of content and its size is the byte length. generate: for i in [start, start+count): path = dir + '/' + prefix*prefix_repeat + zero-padded decimal i (digits wide), or without 'dir/' when dir is empty; content = UTF-8 bytes of the path; mode 420.",
 "limits": {
  "max_entries_per_node": 1024,
  "max_node_bytes": 1048576
 },
